# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Xiaoqing Liu et al. (2026). An AI-ready fine-tuning framework for accurate machine-learning interatomic potentials in solid-solid battery interfaces.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2601.17847  arXiv:2601.17847v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2601.17847v2 (sha256 6d704f0c73dde8f5...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 459 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026ready.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: six battery interface or disordered-electrolyte
# systems, the FIRE workflow (pre-fine-tuning on 20-50 perturbed
# structures, MD candidate pools of about 20,000, SOAP/PCA/k-means
# selection of 500-4,000 representatives, replay-augmented fine-tuning
# of mace-mpa-0-medium) and the one per-model error stated in the text
# (the deployed 2,700-frame Na/Na3SbS4 model). Other errors are given as
# ranges or in figures; diffusion, conductivity and elastic properties
# are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
