###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Per-system FIRE errors are stated only as ranges (energy RMSE 0.1-1.0 meV/atom, force RMSE 8-54 meV/A); per-system values and the from-scratch, random-sampling and vanilla fine-tuning baselines are figure-only (Figs. 2-3). The deployed Na/Na3SbS4 model's evaluation split is in the SI, so its role is null; the Na/Na3SbS4 run here stands for that 2,700-frame model.
# - Diffusion coefficients, conductivities, elastic moduli and stress tests are properties. Literature errors quoted for orientation are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026ready.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

